The other posters have given good tips about going forward!
I think you should consider going back. There are two very
profitable ways to spend your next few thousand turns. Set
up camp at the lowest altar in the dungeon and go through
all your monster creating stuff. You can increase your
mileage by cursing your ?oCM and breaking your /oCM when
it's down to it's last charge. The monsters will bring you
lots of new stuff, maybe the ring you're looking for.
 
When you get "reconciliation" or just "Your sacrifice is
consumed in a burst of flames", it's safe to pray on the
altar. Several good things can happen. All your inventory
may be uncursed, you may get 5 HP, one point of divine
protection or your wielded weapon may be fixed and blessed.
You'll probably get crowned, good and bad to that. The
spellbooks you get from time to time won't be much help to a
barbarian, I expect. Of course, you can make Holy Water as
well, which you could use to uncurse those rings.

Or you could just sacrifice without praying hoping for
artifact weapons.

The other thing you could do is go to every fountain above
DL20 dipping potions, cursed items and scrolls. You might
get a wish but you will certainly uncurse some items and
blank some scrolls and potions.

Did you bypass any sinks? You might get that 14th level
there.

